@startuml
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
scale max 800 width
skinparam padding 2
skinparam ParticipantPadding 20
skinparam maxMessageSize 150

title 3.1 — Content Generation: Caption Matrix & Approval

actor Operator as O
participant "ContentStudio\nView" as UI
participant "Content\nController" as CC
participant "ContentGeneration\nService" as CGS
participant "ContentApproval\nService" as CAS
participant "FastAPI\n(LangGraph Agent)" as FP
participant "tbl_localized_\npromotional_content" as DB

== 1. Content Generation (on mount) ==

O -> UI: Navigate to Content Studio\n(market selected)
UI -> CC: POST /api/v1/content/generate\n{market, businessName, description,\ncategories, trend, ?profileId}

alt profileId provided
  CC -> CGS: generate(req)
  CGS -> CGS: Load BusinessProfile from DB\n(override request body fields)
else no profileId
  CC -> CGS: generate(req)\n(use request body as-is)
end

CGS -> CGS: buildForecastContext()\n(query ForecastResult + MarketScore\nfrom Module 2 tables)

CGS -> FP: POST /internal/content/generate\n{market, businessName, categories,\nuniquenesScore, forecastContext}

note right of FP
  LangGraph 2-node StateGraph:
  Node 1 — analyze_services:
    filter relevant vs extra services
  Node 2 — generate_platform_captions:
    3 archetypes × 3 platforms
    (Witty / Formal / Storytelling)
    × (Instagram / TikTok / Facebook)
  CulturalResearchService provides
    market context (SerpAPI or template)
  Naver captions are hardcoded
    (2 curated Korean blog options)
end note

alt LLM available
  FP --> CGS: ContentResponseDto\n{captions: {platform → archetypes}, source: "llm"}
else LLM unavailable
  FP --> CGS: ContentResponseDto\n{captions: fallback templates, source: "fallback"}
end

CGS -> DB: INSERT 4 rows\n(instagram, tiktok, facebook, naver)\napproval_status = false

CGS --> CC: ContentResponseDto
CC --> UI: ContentResponseDto\n{market, captions, source}
UI -> UI: Render AIContentMatrixPanel\n3 platform tabs × 3 archetype cards

== 2. Content Approval (fire-and-forget) ==

O -> UI: Click "Approve" on one\ncaption per platform
UI ->> CC: POST /api/v1/content/approve\n{profileId, market}\n[non-blocking]

CC -> CAS: approveForMarket(profileId, market)
CAS -> DB: UPDATE approval_status = true\nSET approved_at = now()\nfor all rows matching\n(businessProfileId, selectedMarket)

note right of DB
  This approval gate enables
  Submodule 3.2 Creative Direction.
  hasApprovedContent() checks
  this flag before generating
  visual direction.
end note

DB --> CAS: updated rows
CAS --> CC: void
CC --> UI: {approvedIds, market, count}

@enduml
